   "text": "Read only the page below. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse. Answer each question from the page alone. When the page does not say, answer \"Not stated\".\n\n<<<PAGE\n# release-notes\n\n## What it does\n\nDrafts release notes from merged PRs between two tags. It gathers the PRs and creates the draft; the neighboring `technical-writing` skill edits prose.\n\n## When to use it\n\nUse it when you need a release-notes draft for a tag range. Run it manually:\n\n```text\n/release-notes <from-tag> <to-tag>\n```\n\nBoth tags must exist, and `gh` must be signed in. It stops if `gh auth status` fails or either tag cannot be resolved. A missing tag stops drafting with `TAG_UNRESOLVED`.\n\n## How it works\n\nThe skill gathers merged PRs between the tags and skips PRs labeled `skip-notes`.\n\nIt groups PRs by Conventional Commit type, with features, fixes, and breaking changes first. For PRs with labels naming multiple types, grouping counts the labels using a strict-majority rule. The code breaks ties by label order.\n\nEvery breaking change needs a migration line. If the PR body has none, the draft marks it `TODO: migration`.\n\n## What you get\n\nA `RELEASE_NOTES.md` file in the working tree, grouped by change type and marked with any missing migration guidance.\n\nThe skill stops after writing the draft. It never publishes.\nPAGE>>>\n\nQuestions:\n(a) Will it publish a release?\n(b) How do you run it?\n(c) What happens to a breaking change with no migration note?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"a\": \"...\", \"b\": \"...\", \"c\": \"...\"}. Start the answer to (a) with Yes, No, or Not stated.",
